---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import config from '../data/config.json';
---
<Shell title="Privacy & storage" active="privacy"><article class="prose"><span class="eyebrow">Your browser, your choice</span><h1>Privacy & storage</h1> <p>{config.name} works without signing in. Activity answers, selections, and bookmarks are processed in your browser and are never sent to a server.</p><h2>Optional saved progress</h2><p>Progress is saved only when you enable remembering or explicitly save a bookmark. Theme preferences can also be saved. Each app uses its own storage namespace. No names, email addresses, or account identifiers are requested.</p><p>Stored records are ignored and removed when read after 30 days. localStorage does not automatically delete records while the site is closed. Your browser may clear them sooner. Saved progress is a convenience and is not a durable backup.</p><h2>Clear or avoid storage</h2><p>Use Manage saved data in the footer to clear this app's records and reset the activity. All core activities work when storage is blocked. Downloaded files and copied results are under your control.</p><h2>Anonymous activity counts</h2><p>When you start, finish or share an activity, the page sends an anonymous count to moongazer.tech: the date, the app, the activity id and the event. No cookie, no IP address and no device details are stored, and nothing identifies you. If your browser sends Global Privacy Control, no count is sent.</p> <h2>Feedback you send</h2><p>If you use “Report an error or suggest something”, we store your message, its category, the page address and the date. An email address is stored only if you choose to give one, and it is never published. Messages are read before anything is changed; corrections appear in the public <a href="https://moongazer.tech/corrections/">corrections log</a> without your details.</p> <h2>Hosting and links</h2><p>The hosting provider receives the requests needed to serve the site and may maintain infrastructure logs. This site includes no analytics, advertising or third-party fonts. Opening a source link takes you to that source's own website and privacy practices.</p><h2>Informal scores</h2><p>Scoring is local and meant for personal learning. Browser data and shared text can be edited. There are no public leaderboards.</p><a class="button secondary" href="/">Return to the activity</a></article></Shell>
